# Translation of the Museum of Alternative Displays into Esperanto.
# How to work on this file: TRANSLATING.md at the top of the repository.
# 
# Esperanto. The visitor is addressed as "vi", and instructions are in the imperative.
# A display as a kind of device is a "vidigilo", a picture surface is an "ekrano", and a readout of fixed characters or
# segments is a "montrilo". A hall is a "halo" and a piece is an "eksponaĵo". A pixel is a "bildero".
# A glass tube with a glow in it is a "tubo", so that "valvo" stays free for the light valves of hall 4.
# Names of people stay as they are spelled on the English labels. Figures use a decimal comma.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: Museum of Alternative Displays\n"
"Report-Msgid-Bugs-To: https://github.com/obartra/museum-of-alternative-displays/issues\n"
"Language: eo\n"
"Language-Team: Esperanto\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=2; plural=(n != 1);\n"

